    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0307" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1884</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-20T09:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1916, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Fourth Regiment Marines arrived yesterday and after colonel had interviews with
                    Caperton and myself left here last night for Monte Cristi preparatory to
                    occupying Santiago, Moca and La Vega if necessary. Deadlock continues in the
                    House, no immediate election President seems probable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
